  "election_date": "2026-11-03",
  "description": "Virginia's 8th Congressional District covers Arlington County, the cities of Alexandria and Falls Church, and parts of eastern Fairfax County in Northern Virginia. Incumbent Democrat Don Beyer, first elected in 2014, is seeking a seventh term in this strongly Democratic district (Cook PVI: D+26). Beyer faces a competitive Democratic primary on August 4, 2026, against four challengers including former CIA officer Adam Dunigan, former State Department official Michael Duffin, former Alexandria City Councilmember Mo Seifeldein, and Lorena Bruner. The Republican nominee is Tony Sabio, a former CIA and Secret Service officer. The Virginia Supreme Court struck down a mid-decade redistricting referendum in May 2026, keeping the current district boundaries in place.",
